quadratic in b: B**3*b**2 + B**3*b + B**3 - 3*B*b**2 + 3*B*b + 2*b**2 - 4*b + 2
discriminant: -3*B**2*(B - 1)**3*(B + 3)
B roots: [-3, 0, 1]
section: B= -3 D= 4*I F= 9*I
X= -3*a**2/(b - 1) Y= a*(4*I + 9*I/(b - 1))
Three orbit points lie on Y= -3*I*b/a X + -5*I*a
Line-intersection coefficient identities: [0, 0, 0]
Hence trace_3=O and trace_12=O by the elliptic chord law.
section: B= 0 D= sqrt(2) F= 0
X= 0 Y= sqrt(2)*a
The invariant section is -P; its trace_12 is -12P.
section: B= 1 D= 0 F= sqrt(3)
X= a**2/(b - 1) Y= sqrt(3)*a/(b - 1)
Three orbit points lie on Y= sqrt(3)*b/a X + -sqrt(3)*a
Line-intersection coefficient identities: [0, 0, 0]
Hence trace_3=O and trace_12=O by the elliptic chord law.
Deck action on every ansatz section:
sigma^j Q: X=B*a^2/(b-omega^j), Y=a*(D+omega^j*F/(b-omega^j)); j=0,1,2.
Thus sigma^3 fixes every section in this ansatz, and trace_12=4*trace_3.
